From 4817450e68baba480d3baeb7413fdcf7299a8fd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:45:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH RFC] powerpc/ps3: Don't pause a thread with an interrupt
 already pending

ps3_power_save() calls lv1_pause(0) soft-disabled, with MSR[EE] on. A
decrementer interrupt that fires between the idle loop's
local_irq_disable() and the hcall is masked: masked_interrupt sets DEC
to 0x7fffffff (27 s at the 79.8 MHz timebase) and records PACA_IRQ_DEC
for the replay. The thread then pauses with no decrementer to wake it,
and every timer queued on it (the tick, hrtimers, timer-wheel timers)
waits for the next external interrupt.

ps3_virq_setup() binds all PS3_BINDING_CPU_ANY interrupts to thread 0,
which therefore recovers within milliseconds. Thread 1 only receives
IPIs and can stay asleep for seconds. In practice this showed up as
games freezing for 0.3 to 4 s with the CPU idle: the fence poll of an
out-of-tree GPU driver is an hrtimer on the waiter's CPU, and the idle
loop was entered 4000 times a second.

Measured on a PS3 (two PPE threads, 6.12 kernel, periodic tick), two
120 s runs with both threads idle and a SCHED_FIFO task pinned to each
thread, sleeping 20 ms at a time:

  nothing else running:     thread 1 woke up to 1439 ms late (13 wakeups
                            100 ms or more late, 2 over 1 s); thread 0
                            at most 16.7 ms late
  a 10 ms timer kick (an    thread 1 at most 19.4 ms late, none over
  IPI to each thread):      100 ms

Waking the thread often hides the problem, which fits a decrementer
that was pushed out and not delivered.

Use prep_irq_for_idle(), as pseries_lpar_idle() and cbe_power_save()
do: it hard-disables and returns false when something was masked, in
which case we return without pausing and the replay in
local_irq_enable() runs it. Otherwise pause with MSR[EE] on, the state
the hcall is entered in today, so from the check on a decrementer or IPI
is taken as a normal interrupt and re-arms the decrementer.

Pausing with MSR[EE] off (prep_irq_for_idle_irqsoff(), as powernv does)
would close the last window too, but it relies on lv1_pause() ending on
a decrementer that is pending while MSR[EE] is off, and on the
hypervisor keeping that exception pending for the guest. Neither is
documented beyond "MSR[EE] has no effect". With MSR[EE] on, the one race
left is an interrupt handled between the hard-enable and the hcall: one
that set need_resched is caught by the check just before lv1_pause(),
and otherwise the pause ends at the next timer event, not seconds later.

Signed-off-by: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
---
 arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c b/arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c
index 5144f11..1ff77a9 100644
--- a/arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c
+++ b/arch/powerpc/platforms/ps3/setup.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <linux/export.h>
 #include <linux/memblock.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/sched.h>
 
 #include <asm/machdep.h>
 #include <asm/firmware.h>
@@ -22,6 +23,7 @@
 #include <asm/udbg.h>
 #include <asm/lv1call.h>
 #include <asm/ps3gpu.h>
+#include <asm/hw_irq.h>
 
 #include "platform.h"
 
@@ -64,9 +66,29 @@ static void ps3_power_save(void)
 	 * lv1_pause() puts the PPE thread into inactive state until an
 	 * irq on an unmasked plug exists. MSR[EE] has no effect.
 	 * flags: 0 = wake on DEC interrupt, 1 = ignore DEC interrupt.
+	 *
+	 * The idle loop calls us soft-disabled with MSR[EE] on. A decrementer
+	 * that fires in that state is masked: the masked handler pushes DEC
+	 * out to 0x7fffffff and leaves PACA_IRQ_DEC set for the replay, so a
+	 * pause entered after that sleeps through every timer of this thread
+	 * until some other interrupt arrives. Device interrupts are all bound
+	 * to thread 0, so thread 1 may get nothing but IPIs.
+	 *
+	 * prep_irq_for_idle() hard-disables and returns false when something
+	 * was masked since local_irq_disable(); returning then lets the replay
+	 * in local_irq_enable() run it. Otherwise pause with MSR[EE] on, as
+	 * before, so that a decrementer or IPI from here on is taken as a
+	 * normal interrupt. Interrupts are enabled with the hcall, so one
+	 * that made a task runnable just before it is caught by need_resched().
 	 */
 
-	lv1_pause(0);
+	if (!prep_irq_for_idle())
+		return;
+
+	__hard_irq_enable();
+
+	if (!need_resched())
+		lv1_pause(0);
 }
 
 static void __noreturn ps3_restart(char *cmd)
-- 
